1. every value has a class
   1.class                        Integer
   nil.class                      NilClass
   true.class                     TrueClass
   Integer.class                  Class
   Class.class                    Class
2. an operator is a method call
   1 + 2                          3
   1.+(2)                         3
   1.send(:+, 2)                  3
3. nil is an object with methods
   nil.to_a                       []
   nil.to_s                       ""
   nil.inspect                    "nil"
4. a literal is a receiver
   3.times.to_a                   [0, 1, 2]
   "a".upcase                     "A"
   1.class (no parentheses)       Integer
5. the ancestor chain
   Integer.ancestors              [Integer, Numeric, Comparable, Object, Kernel, BasicObject]
   NilClass.ancestors             [NilClass, Object, Kernel, BasicObject]
6. everything is an Object, classes included
   1.is_a?(Object)                true
   nil.is_a?(Object)              true
   Integer.is_a?(Object)          true
   Integer.is_a?(Class)           true
7. even the top level is an object
   self.inspect                   "main"
   self.class                     Object
8. what a small integer cannot do
   1.singleton_class              TypeError
